# KPI Starter UX

Product target: **site / business KPIs for marketing & growth** — not engineering productivity (Findy). Borrow Findy **readability & hierarchy** only; copy, IA, and data sources must stay distinct.

Rules can be edited anytime in this file; changes apply to later chats.

## Settled product direction (do not reopen lightly)

These decisions are **locked** for the current product. Prefer growing packs/metrics inside this frame over redesigning the frame.

1. **One product story** — Marketing/growth site + business KPIs. Not eng-productivity / Findy framing.
2. **One dense board for all packs** — Same layout for every industry; only DEMO numbers, event vocabulary, 業界目安, and pack copy change.
3. **Board order = depth of the question, not user level (2026-11 redesign)** — one page, top → bottom: **L0 いまの状態** (one-sentence verdict + 3 tiles: 主転換の件数 · 主転換率 · 一番の課題, each with 前期 and 業界 in words) → **L1 どこで離れているか** (行動フロー as a compact funnel + 今見るべきこと + 流入別) → **L2 詳しい数字** (tabs: 転換ファネル · エンゲージ · 流入チャネル · オーディエンス · イベント · 業務KPI). Beginners stop at L0–L1; intermediates go down to L2. No beginner/advanced mode switch.
4. **Display language** — In-app **設定** stores session `locale` (`ja` / `en` / `ko`). Translates **UI chrome** (nav, table headers, 説明, panels) **and pack-owned spoken labels** (指標名, 業界パック名, 説明 body, next-watch). GA event ids (`apply_complete`) and channel group names (`Organic Search`) stay as-is — never as chips under summary values or in the 重点 banner.
5. **Data honesty** — Sample packs ≠ live. Live = GA4 numbers + chosen pack’s 目安/labels only. Unlinked 業務 = `—`. Always show period / property / pack identity.
6. **Nav IA** — Top-level groups: **マイサイト** · **ツール** · **見本**, plus **設定** at the bottom. No pack search, no long pack tree.
   - マイサイト: `/live` (when connected) · `/setup` (サイトの設定) · `/connect` (接続・切断), or a GA4 connect CTA when unconnected
   - ツール: `/builder` · `/glossary`
   - 見本: `/samples` (見本ボード一覧) + the sample currently being viewed (indent only). **Do not** put `/beginner` or `/first` in the rail — `/beginner` may stay as a direct URL; `/first` now only redirects to `/live` (the board's いまの状態 is the first scene)
7c. **行動フロー** — In L1 (after いまの状態, next to 今見るべきこと): サイトに来た → the pack's behaviour steps (`packs/flows.py`) as linked nodes, each with users, 来た人の %, and 次へ / 離脱 % on the arrow; the biggest drop is marked; 全体/channel switch (top 4 + その他) and 流入別 reach to the last measured step. Live counts are GA4 users; untracked steps say 未計測 and clicking a step maps the site's own event name (per property, also aliases イベント and 主転換). Samples are labelled 見本 and can't be mapped. Live boards can put up to 3 other behaviours (別の行動) above or below a step — ＋ appears only in 編集モード (`流れを直す` / `.where.is-editing`); event + optional name; shows users and % from the previous step; edit/delete in its popover; stored per property. They never change the main path or its conversion. Already-added branches stay visible outside edit mode. The flow is one row of columns (vertical bar = 来た人の %, scrolls sideways when tight) and stacks vertically only on phones (container < 700px).
  **Entry (numbers-first, 2026-11):** `/` (connect · デモで試す · 見本) → `/connect` (sign-in + property) → **`/live` at once**. If no flow is chosen yet, `/live` guesses the behaviour from the site's GA4 events (`selection.guess_behavior`: purchase > sign_up > form_submit > video_complete > click, then how many of the flow's steps the site records; nothing → ブログ) and the industry via `default_industry`, and shows a 仮 notice (「サイトに合わせる」→ `/setup`, 「このままでよい」→ POST `/setup/keep`). Demo: `/connect/demo?start=1` is one click to a board. **サイトの設定** has no pages: the board's 「どこで離れているか」 has an 編集モード (`/live?edit=1`, board/edit_bar.html + board_edit.js; click a step → right-top drawer) and the top bar has a 「比べる業種」 drawer (`/live?industry=1`). `/setup*` GETs redirect there; POST errors come back as a session flash. **Rules:** the screen shows numbers · verdicts · one line; supplementary text goes into 「説明」 popovers. Only two overlay kinds: 説明 popover / 指標辞典 card dialog, and the right-top drawer. 詳しい数字 is every category stacked (no tabs) with 8週の推移, from `board/extras.py`; live boards load it from `/live/details`. Industry: the drawer; 業界目安 only when a published benchmark exists (`packs/derived.py` + `packs/sources.py`). Never put a wizard before the first numbers. One decision per setup screen.
  7b. **今見るべきこと** — In L1 beside 流入別: up to 3 metrics furthest outside their 業界目安 (worse first, then better), each with value · 目安 · 差, 自社の前期 and a tip. Never fill it with filler when nothing is off — say so. The worst one is also L0's 一番の課題 tile; with none, that tile is the flow's biggest drop. (かんたん/詳細 mode and 次に見るポイント were tried and removed — do not bring them back without asking.)
  7d. **Two yardsticks** — every rate/count carries both 業界目安 and 自社の前期比 (real previous period: GA4 prev range on /live, deterministic `board/prev.py` for samples; pt for rates, % for counts; colour by better/worse, never invented — “—” when unknown). L0 says both in words (前期より改善 / 目安内 …) with the numbers small; L2 rows show 前期比 + one judge chip and open for 業界目安 · 目安差.
7e. **Fewer numbers, same rules** — One number + one judge chip per row; 業界目安 · 目安差 · 意味 · 説明 open with the row (帯 only in the tooltip / popover). 流入チャネル shows top 5 + 「その他（n）」. イベント shows 10 + 「ほか n 件」. 業務KPI collapses to one line while every row is unlinked.
7. **Connect path** — Property → `/live` always (guess + 仮 notice when nothing is chosen). Live board uses GA4 numbers + selection’s behaviour (flow/labels) × industry (業界目安). Do not copy sample DEMO business numbers into `/live`.

## Core

1. **Metric names are the shared language** — Primary on-screen label = what the team says out loud (`登録CVR`, `Organic Search`, `申込完了`). Do not replace them with long paraphrase titles. Raw GA event ids are secondary vocabulary for 説明 / イベント rows, not summary decoration.
2. **Explanations via「説明」** — Keep the row clean (name + value + 前期比 + judge). 「説明」 opens 意味 / 計算式 / 見るポイント (not `?`); in L2 it sits in the opened row (「説明を開く」), in L0 tiles and 今見るべきこと it sits beside the name. Put GA event id, formula detail, and beginner glosses **inside 説明** — do not bury the screen in one-line glosses or summary `code` chips. Only the 主転換 tag may sit on a row; no other per-row category chips.
3. **Maximize useful information** — Prefer dense tables/lists over sparse decorative cards. Cards only when they aid scanning or interaction.
4. **L0 pops** — One sentence a beginner can repeat to a boss, then three big numbers with 前期 / 業界 in words. Do not cram tables, tips, or event-id chips into L0. No separate 重点 banner (the sentence replaces it).

## Structure & copy

5. **One purpose per section** — いまの状態 (is it OK?) → どこで離れているか (where does it leak?) → 詳しい数字 (why / evidence). Do not break this order or mix purposes in one block.
5b. **Tab order tells a story** — 転換ファネル → エンゲージ → 流入チャネル → オーディエンス → イベント → 業務KPI (convert → depth → where from → who → evidence → business reality). The last opened tab is remembered per browser; `#panel-<id>` opens a tab.
5c. **One dense board for all industry packs** — `/{slug}` uses the same `/sample` layout; only DEMO numbers, event names, 業界目安 bands, and pack copy (CVR label etc.) change. Do not maintain a separate card UI per industry. New industries = new `sitekpi/packs/{slug}.py` + registry entry.
5d. **Nav categories stay separate** — Sidebar groups: **マイサイト** (live / setup / connect) · **ツール** (builder / glossary) · **見本** (samples gallery + current sample). Never mix sample packs into the connected-property list; never put `/beginner` or `/first` in the rail.
5e. **見本ボード** — `/samples` lists behaviours → industries; viewing a sample shows that pack indented under 見本. Dense board layout is shared; only DEMO / labels / 目安 change per pack.
5f. **接続後は行動 × 業種 → 目安のみ適用** — After property + setup, session stores behaviour + industry. `/live` uses **GA4 live numbers** + behaviour flow/labels + industry **BENCHMARKS only**. Never copy sample DEMO revenue・会員・業務数字 into the live board. Meta must show the selection / 業界目安. If setup incomplete while connected, send to `/first` (not back to property pick alone).
6. **UI language** — Product chrome follows session locale (default Japanese). Primary metric vocabulary stays the spoken industry terms (JP pack copy for now). GA event/channel ids appear where that id *is* the catalog name (イベント表) or inside 説明 — not competing with spoken labels in the summary.
7. **Discoverability** — When catalogs are large: search, “値ありだけ”, collapsible groups. The board has **no per-section view modes** any more (リスト/カード/バー/比較/トレンド were removed in the 2026-11 redesign): each L2 tab is one table (指標 · 値 · 前期比 · 判定) whose rows open. 流入チャネル adds one stacked bar above its table; イベント shows a small share bar under each count. 指標辞典 `/glossary` cards keep equal height **and aligned internal rows** (title · 意味 · 計算 · 見る) — prefer CSS subgrid over ragged wrap. Sample-pack sidebar uses category `<details>`. Optional **metric stickers** (cute mascot loops): add `static/stickers/{HELP_id}.gif` (+ optional `.png` still); glossary shows them when present, no sticker = layout unchanged; language-agnostic; grow one metric at a time — do not require a full set.

## Data honesty

8. **GA4 = live path; industry packs = samples** — Never present demo revenue/membership as live after GA4 connect. Selecting a pack on connect applies **業界目安 bands** (and board vocabulary), not sample KPI values.
9. **Business KPIs unlinked = explicit** — Show `—` + 業務DB (or equivalent). Do not fill with fake numbers when connected.
10. **Period, property & industry pack visible** — Always show which Property, date range, and (for samples) which **業界パック** the numbers belong to. Prefer **vertical industry names with a domain hint** (`人事・採用`, `建設・住宅`, `会員・サブスク`, …) over jargon-only labels (`B2C`, bare `人事`). On sample boards: **h1 / `<title>` = pack name**; meta line = role + property + period (e.g. `業界パック見本 · 採用 Demo JP · 直近28日`). On `/live`: meta includes `業界目安: {pack}`. Sample-pack nav may show a one-line funnel hint under the name (`求人〜応募`). Never leave the board looking like anonymous live data when it is pack sample.
11. **業界目安 (industry standard) is mandatory — and honest** — For every comparable rate/ratio KPI where a pack standard exists, always show the 業界目安 and 目安差. Cited values come from `packs/sources.py` (link + segment + value, band rule labelled 'SiteKPI の設定'); cited figures that only exist for all industries are marked 「出典・全業種」 (orange) with a note; everything else shows 「基準なし」 (grey, never judged, empty 自社目安 inputs) and its popover explains why there is no standard — never invent a number. Users set 自社目安 in a small popover anchored at the clicked 業界目安 value (or the 目安を調整 list; source shown as a 「出典」 button, never a raw URL; per GA4 property for /live, per browser for samples); the board then labels it 自社目安 / 自社 and judges with it.
12. **Show the verdict, keep the gap one tap away** — Every comparable row shows a judge chip (良好 / 目安内 / 要注意; 基準なし opens why); 目安差 (e.g. `+0.3pt`) and the 業界目安 value are in L0 tiles and in the opened L2 row. The chip is the beginner cue; the number stays — never replace it.
13. **Same chrome whether 目安 exists or not** — Every L2 row has the same four cells (指標 · 値 · 前期比 · 判定) and the same opened part; with no standard the 判定 cell is 「基準なし」 (opens why) or `—` (counts / unlinked). Never drop the cell so some rows look different.
14. **Wide-layout tables** — L2 tables use full width with `table-layout: fixed` (指標 ~46%, the three numeric cells share the rest) and scroll sideways inside their box on phones. Do not leave a dead spacer column.

## Still open (decide when needed; do not invent a new product direction)

- How far `/live` should **propose pack event→GA4 event mapping** beyond 目安 + labels (user override likely).
- Fine-tuning of column proportions on ultra-wide screens.
- Real daily series for `/live` (a trend line could come back inside an opened L2 row, not as a view mode).
- A whole-board channel filter (today the channel switch changes the 行動フロー and 流入別 only).
- Fixed first-number set per behaviour (today: 主転換 · 主転換率 · 一番の課題 for every behaviour).

## Settled polish (keep)

- Sample-pack rail **search** filters name/hint; matching categories open.
- Connect / builder **chrome** follows session locale (same as board).

## Anti-patterns

- Replacing metric names with long paraphrase titles (breaks shared vocabulary)
- Showing GA event ids as summary chips or in the 重点 banner (belongs in 説明 / イベント明細)
- Card-per-KPI walls that reduce information density
- Metric names with no「説明」help (hard for beginners)
- Confusing `?` icon instead of readable「説明」
- Per-row category chips that dilute the metric name
- Long inline explanations that compete with the metric name
- Mixing Findy/dev-productivity framing into product copy
- Stuffing L0 with secondary metrics or tips
- Putting a setup wizard (or an empty step editor) before the first numbers
- Showing every section open at the same weight (that was the old board: 60+ numbers before a verdict)
- KPI rows with value only — no judge chip, or no way to open 業界目安 / 目安差
- Treating 前期比 alone as enough context (前期比 ≠ 業界目安)
- Mixing sample DEMO business numbers into `/live`
- Flattening all sample packs into one long nav list with no categories
- Leaving the sample-pack rail unscrolled / all categories forced open
- Dense card grids (指標辞典) where sibling cards only match outer height but title/意味/計算/見る rows rag differently across the row

13. **Menu** — マイサイト (`/live` when connected, `/setup`, `/connect` or GA4 CTA), ツール (`/builder`, `/glossary`), 見本 (`/samples` + current sample indent only — **no** `/beginner`), 設定 at the bottom. No pack search, no long pack tree. `/first` is post-connect only (not a rail item).

14. **Flows start with GA4 basics** — every flow is サイトに来た (sessions + 流入元 by channel) → session_start (サイトを開いた) → user_engagement (しっかり見た（10秒以上）), worldwide. Behaviour flows have 5–6 steps by default and use GA4's automatically collected / enhanced-measurement / recommended events (user_engagement, scroll, click, view_search_results, file_download, form_start, form_submit, view_item, add_to_cart, begin_checkout, purchase, sign_up, login) so most sites already record them; the board's 主転換 and rates follow the behaviour's own events (`packs/behaviors.py` → board). Industry-specific events stay in industry packs and are reached through the flow editor (`/setup`) or the board's mapping.
